# Pages served by the new Next.js app (127.0.0.1:3300) instead of the PHP site.
# Apache reads this file through `RewriteMap softsuaveSite` in
# apache.softsuave.example.conf. Format: "<exact path> app". No trailing slash:
# the PHP .htaccess already 301s "/x/" to "/x" before the lookup sees it again.
#
# Switch in batches: copy one batch at a time into the server's
# /etc/apache2/softsuave-site-pages.map. Apache re-reads the file when it changes
# (no reload needed). To roll a page back to PHP, delete or comment its line.
#
# Not listed on purpose:
#   /404, /410            PHP keeps its own error pages (ErrorDocument 404 /404.php).
#   /home-v2              a design preview, noindex; not a live URL.
# Everything else on www.softsuave.com (the blog, /forms, the unmigrated PHP pages,
# the old /ad/* pages, robots.txt, sitemap.xml) is not in this file and stays as it is.

